# ffi/logs/rust/stage3-M4-M7.log
# W3 stage 3 parts 4 to 7: M4 (the adapter site), M5 (bulk bytes and the
# direct-argument path), M6 (packed) and M7 (interleaved repeated fields).
# With this, every shape and every payload of design/SHAPES.md is covered.
# 2026-09-18
#
# CONFIGURATION (R7)
#   machine        4 vCPU Intel Xeon @ 2.80GHz, 15 GB, Ubuntu 24.04.4, Linux 6.18.44 x86_64,
#                  container. No CPU pinning, no governor control.
#   rust           rustc/cargo 1.94.1, release. MSRV 1.88 declared, NOT verified.
#   incumbent      prost 0.14.4
#   LINKAGE        cdylib (libak_core.so), dynamic linker. Not a static link.
#   guard          on.  content set: ascii.
#
# CLASS IS PER ROW, NOT PER TABLE (design/SHAPES.md)
#   M4 TaskSummary            REAL     the only `with` adapter in the Rust crate
#   M5 UploadResultData       REAL     the result upload and download path
#   M6 ticks/values/codes/flags  CONTROL  the schema has no packed scalar at all
#   M6 statuses               REAL     the schema's 3 packed fields are all enums
#   M7 DualResponse           CONTROL  legal wire no group buffer keyed by type decodes
#   M6 is therefore a MIXED table and is labelled as one; quoting P6.1 as a control
#   result or as a real one would both be wrong.
#
# M7 IS DECODE ONLY
#   No canonical writer can produce its bytes, so no arm is asked to. The check is that
#   all four arms decode the committed vector to the same value and that a contiguous
#   re-encode is a PERMUTATION of the same (tag, wire type, body) triples, which is the
#   method stage 1 used and the only statement that can be made about it.
#
# THE DIRECT-ARGUMENT PATH (ABI v1 section 8), AND WHAT RUST CANNOT SAY ABOUT IT
#   Built: ak_str.data carries AK_STR_DIRECT and the bytes are an argument of the call.
#   Its value is on the JVM, where the host holds GetPrimitiveArrayCritical or FFM's
#   critical(true) across the whole call -- which it can only do if the codec makes no
#   reverse call, hence the refusal below. ON A RUST HOST IT BUYS NOTHING: there is no
#   pinning to avoid and the copy is a copy either way. So this slice shows the path
#   works and CANNOT confirm the win; the P5.3 and P5.4 rows are not evidence for it.
#
# HAZARDS (R9)
#   - The adapter section is checked by STATE, not by payload, because P4.1 exercises
#     only the one case that works. Its rows come from hand-written facade code.
#   - 4 shared vCPUs; ratios are formed in one process from interleaved rounds (R4).
#   - P5.3 and P5.4 are one element of 1 MB and 4 MB; their rows are a memcpy figure.

